  "description": "The Black-crowned Night Heron is a stocky, short-necked heron that often rests quietly in waterside vegetation by day and becomes more active around dusk. Adults have a black crown and back, gray wings, white underparts, and red eyes, while immatures are brown with pale spotting and streaking. It hunts in freshwater, brackish, and coastal wetlands, standing still or wading slowly before striking at fish, crustaceans, and other prey. It nests in colonies and is found across much of the world, including Hawaii, where it is known as the ʻAukuʻu.",
